  "Description": {
    "Cost": 1040738,
    "UIName": "Jackrabbit",
    "Id": "chassisdef_jackrabbit_JKR-9W",
    "Name": "Jackrabbit",
    "Details": "Conceived as a long-range infantry support Mech, the ill-fated Jackrabbit entered prototyping mere weeks before the Amaris Coup. Mass produced without regard for its design flaws, the 25 ton Jackrabbit suffered from anaemic firepower and poor armor; resulting in a bad reputation and the eventual extinction of the design. Powered by a 150-rated Fusion Engine, the Jackrabbit carries 3.5 tons of Ferro-Fibrous armor and has a top speed of 97 km/h. An endosteel skeleton allows the Jackrabbit JKR-9W to carry a Light AC/5 and a Streak SRM-2, both with a single ton of ammo. An ER Medium Laser rounds out the weapons.\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Quirk: Nimble</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Drop Cost Multiplier: 0.98</color></b>\n\n<color=#FFEF00>Arm Actuator Limits: Left Lower, Right Lower</color>",
